    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0117" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg57"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February 5,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 210.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 326 of December
                    last and your No. 329 of the 1st ultimo, reporting the wounding by Brazilian
                    soldiers of three sailors from the American schooner <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Isaiah K. Stetson</hi> at Santa Catharina and the subsequent death of one
                    of them.</p>
                <p>Your action is approved and the full report of the investigation promised by the
                    Brazilian Government is awaited.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
